# Recipe 14.9 - Self-improving prompt via macro + judge (novel)
# Goal: run a macro prompt, judge the output, use the critique to author an improved macro, reload, re-run, A/B.
# Run: /script doc/cookbook/14_9_self_improve_macro.chatdsl
# Combines: macros (def/%) + /reloadmacros + judge + filebank compare (no repo example invokes macros at all)
# Requires: my_macros.chatdsl defining expert_answer(topic)

# Round 1: baseline macro
/reloadmacros my_macros.chatdsl
/model mistral_1
%expert_answer(rust ownership)
/save 14_9_r1.txt
/filebank1 14_9_r1.txt

# Judge rewrites the prompt template as a new def statement
/model gemini_flash
/multiline
Critique this answer about rust ownership for technical correctness and clarity. Output ONLY a rewritten, better prompt template that would fix the weaknesses, in the form: def expert_answer(topic) = "..."
;;
/multiline
/save my_macros_v2.chatdsl

# Round 2: swap in the improved macro and re-run
/reloadmacros my_macros_v2.chatdsl
/model mistral_1
%expert_answer(rust ownership)
/save 14_9_r2.txt
/filebank2 14_9_r2.txt

/model gemini_flash
/multiline
Compare {filebank1} (round 1) and {filebank2} (round 2). Did the rewritten prompt improve the answer? Score both 0-10.
;;
/multiline
/save 14_9_verdict.txt
